   20   Unreachable case: C_ATR trajectories + zoom [115,120] min
          run_unreachable_example2.m
          -> unreachable_results/fig_unreachable_trajectory_zoom.{png,eps}
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  NOTE: plot_figure16_redraw.m and fig16_comparison.* are HISTORICAL
        file names. They plot what is Figure 18 in the current
        manuscript (weighted errors WITH the Theorem-3 bound).
        plot_results.m "Fig. 9" is a simplified version of Figure 18
        WITHOUT the bound. Use plot_figure16_redraw.m for the paper.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. PAPER TABLES  <->  GENERATING SCRIPTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tab.  Description                              Script / Output
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1    Main notation                            (theoretical, no code)

   2    Cross-validation results of DyPLS-MIMO-ARX
          run_stage02_identification.m (stdout + stage02_log.txt)

   3    Free-run on independent test set (batch-wise)
          run_stage02_identification.m (stdout + stage02_log.txt)

   4    SISO-ARX vs MIMO-ARX comparison          (manual, not in branch)

   5    alpha / beta sensitivity of tube margins
          compute_invariant_ellipsoid.m (Inv.Sens)
          printed by export_tables.m via run_diagnostics_example2.m
          -> results/diagnostics/out/tables/Metrics_Tables.txt (Tab.3a,3b)

   6    Per-batch tracking errors at reference points
          derived from Data_prop.Err_true_act / Err_opt_nom
          stored in results/stage05_simulation.mat

   7    Monte-Carlo robustness table             (not in this branch)

   8    Physical / kinetic parameters            init_params.m

   9    Simulation & identification parameters
          run_diagnostics_example2.m
          -> results/diagnostics/out/tables/table_params.txt

   10   PLS evidence per component (EV_X, EV_Y, sigma_min(Q), rank)
          report_pls_evidence_example2.m via run_diagnostics_example2.m
          (console Tables A/B/C)

   11   QP Hessian condition number (raw vs latent)
          compute_qp_conditioning.m via run_diagnostics_example2.m
          (console)

   12   Reference vs optimal reachable points
          compute_optimal_reachable.m (stdout)
          -> results/diagnostics/out/tables/table_reachable_points.txt

   13   Effect of A_lv, n_arx on VAF / NRMSE / tightening / reachability
          run_sensitivity_A.m   ->  sensitivity_A_data.csv
          *** SLOW: retrains the model on a 5x3 grid. ***

   14   Oh [13] Q_trk / R_upd 3x3 sensitivity
          run_oh_sensitivity_sweep.m
          -> oh_sensitivity_results.txt
             oh_sensitivity_workspace.mat
          then sweep_main.m for max-adjacent-batch metrics.

   15   Parameter configuration of the three methods
          (not in code — see manuscript Table 15)

   16   Performance & computational cost of the three methods
          report_simulation_comparison.m (console)
          export_comparison_table.m via run_stage06_reporting.m
          -> results/reporting/comparison_table.csv
             results/reporting/batch_metrics.csv

   17   Active constraints in the unreachable scenario
          run_unreachable_example2.m
          -> unreachable_results/table_unreachable_active.csv
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. NOTES FOR REVIEWERS / READERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Reproducibility. Random seeds are centralised in init_params.m:
        rng_seed       — training data
        rng_seed_val   — validation data
        rng_seed_unc   — calibration data
        rng_seed_online— shared closed-loop scenario (identical for all
                         three controllers).

  * Comparable weights. All three controllers share
        Q_trk = 100 ,  R_upd = 1e-4
    (see init_params.m and Section 6-C of the paper).

  * Unreachable scenario. run_unreachable_example2.m OVERRIDES
    Params.y_ref_phys(2) = 0.013 and rebuilds the nominal problem.
    It does NOT overwrite stage03_tube.mat or stage05_simulation.mat;
    its outputs go to unreachable_results/.

  * Numerical safeguards. solve_qp_checked.m guards against non-convex
    Hessians, scaled infeasibility and non-optimal QP exits, and
    gracefully accepts status = 3 (max iterations) when the returned
    point is feasible.

  * Missing artefacts. Each stage verifies the presence of the previous
    .mat file; running run_stage06_reporting from an empty results/
    folder fails with a clear message.

  * Wood-Berry example (Figs 2–9, Table 4). This lives in the separate
    branch Wood_Berry_Column of the upstream repository
        https://github.com/ChaoMpc/Batch-wise_Optimization_Control.git
    The current working directory corresponds to the
        Batch-Crystallization
    branch.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9. QUICK CHECKLIST
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  [ ] Octave >= 8 installed;  control, optim, glpk loadable.
  [ ] Working directory = folder that contains all *.m files.
  [ ] results/*.mat present           -> use SECTION 4 (fast).
      -- OR --
      you accept the 1–2 h runtime    -> use SECTION 3 (full pipeline).

  Reproduce the paper figures:
  [ ] run_stage06_reporting        -> Figures 10–17, Table 16
  [ ] run_diagnostics_example2     -> Figure 18 (with Theorem 3 bound),
                                      Tables 5, 9, 10, 11, 12
  [ ] run_unreachable_example2     -> Figures 19, 20, Table 17
  [ ] run_oh_sensitivity_sweep     -> Table 14

  Optional / slow:
  [ ] run_sensitivity_A            -> Table 13 (retrains 300 batches)
  [ ] run_nominal_openloop_check   -> console diagnostic
  [ ] run_fast_pipeline            -> only after editing init_params.m
                                      (A_lv, n_arx MUST be unchanged)

